# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every
# platform. Without this, Git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default)
# rewrites files to CRLF when cloning, which breaks two things:
#
#   * data/prompts.json is generated with explicit LF endings so it is
#     byte-identical across operating systems, and a test asserts it contains
#     no CR bytes. A CRLF checkout would fail that test on a fresh clone.
#   * the dataset's SHA-256 would differ per platform, defeating the
#     reproducible-generation guarantee documented in the README.
* text=auto eol=lf
